# Every env file except the committed example. Listed exhaustively rather than
# as `.env*` so that `.env.example` stays tracked, and rather than as the three
# Next.js happens to document — `.env.production` was missing, which is the one
# a real key is most likely to end up in.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.development
.env.production
.env.test

